    <string name="start_a_walk_and_allow_precise_location_the_map_is_revealed_in_a_" formatted="false">"Start a walk and allow precise location. The map is revealed in a continuous trail along your route, up to 100 m with walls taken into account. GPS accuracy is shown as a separate circle.\n\nRecording continues with the screen off until you tap “Stop”. Progress is stored only on your phone.\n\nWorld outlines are available offline. Save streets and satellite imagery with “Download offline area”. While the map is open, your location and colours update automatically. Walk recording keeps working with the screen off."</string>
    <string name="gps_accuracy_within_30_m_speed_up_to_4_5_m_s_with_additional_accu" formatted="false">"GPS: accuracy within 30 m; speed up to 4.5 m/s with additional accuracy checks. GPS jumps and mock locations do not reveal the map.\n\nOffline: connect vector MBTiles (OpenMapTiles/Protomaps MVT/PBF) or raster MBTiles. Detailed maps use the atlas style. The planet file stays on your phone; only needed sections are read. Raw OSM PBF and PMTiles are unsupported.\n\nStreets: © OpenStreetMap contributors, openstreetmap.org/copyright. Only visible sections are loaded. “Download offline area” saves streets and buildings via Overpass, with optional EOX satellite imagery.\n\nLocal MBTiles show vector streets, buildings, water and names in the atlas. Satellite imagery is a separate mode and is not included in vector files. Overview imagery is about 10 m/pixel, from 2016. EOxCloudless https://cloudless.eox.at by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2016), CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . OSM licence: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright . Download providers receive the selected area bounds. Walk coordinates stay local."</string>
